WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.940
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament Finals.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.370
In Dande and Satoshi’s struggle over
the summit of Pokémon battling,

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.240
Dande currently has
three Pokémon left,

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.620
while Satoshi is one step ahead,
with four.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.750
However, all of Satoshi’s Pokémon
have already taken heavy damage.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.260
Though he appears to have the lead,
Satoshi has actually been driven into a corner.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.430
How will Satoshi fight back in this,
the single biggest Pokémon battle in history?

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.570
Kairyu, watch out!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.870
You can do it, Kairyu!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.490
Go for it, Satoshi!

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.750
Big Bro! Fight!

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.410
Drum Attack!

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.090
Hurricane!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.600
He starts an intense Hurricane!

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:19.310
The Flying-type move is super effective
on the Grass-type Gorillander!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.880
An astonishing Drum Attack
reduces Hurricane’s damage!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.750
All right!

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.920
You can do that?

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.260
That’s more like a Gentle Breeze
than a Hurricane.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.470
That won’t do any damage, meow.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.060
Go snap those roots
like they’re twigs!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.150
Do it!

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.590
Kairyu, you okay?!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.590
Her speed dropped... Drum Attack's doing, I take it?

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.560
When I send out a Grass type,
my opponents tend to attack it with Flying-type moves,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.390
so that was my counter.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.150
“The best defense
is a good offense...”

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.650
Mr. Dande’s kinda like Satoshi.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.530
Huh?

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.740
Don’t you think
their battle styles are similar?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.780
Now, show me more, Satoshi!

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.910
Then...

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.080
Let’s do it!
Dra-Kairyu Meteor!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:36.420
There it is! The move that took down Drapult,
Dra-Kairyu Meteor!

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.840
Gorillander!
Use Drum Attack!

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.230
Break through!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.650
What?!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.650
Too bad, Satoshi.
I knew you’d play it like that!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.160
Ooh, it’s just like Vine Whip.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.390
Finish it, Kairyu!
Use Dragon Claw!

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.980
Acrobatics!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.740
So fast!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.660
What the...?
That’s a <i>move?</i>

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.250
It’s way too nimble
for its size, meow.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.140
Kairyu!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.020
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.650
His type disadvantage
did not matter one bit!

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.610
Is this how a Champion battles?!

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.820
Big Bro!

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.410
And with that, it’s now a 3v3.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.160
Who will Satoshi pick?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.740
Return, Kairyu.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.040
You put up a great fight.
Have a nice, long rest.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:38.380
Come out, Negigaknight!

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.380
It’s Negigaknight!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.760
Star Assault!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.850
100,000 Horsepower!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.900
And they clash!
Are they evenly matched?!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.030
Hold out!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.160
Push!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.170
All right!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.060
Gorillander stands back up!

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:45.740
But the recoil from Star Assault
leaves Negigaknight unable to attack!

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.080
100,000 Horsepower!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.090
Negigaknight,
ride your shield!

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.510
Drum Attack!

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.730
Consecutive Cut!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:24.190
Acrobatics!

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.140
Negigaknight is unable to battle!

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:00.770
That’s my big bro!

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.900
Back-to-back losses
for Competitor Satoshi!

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:07.780
Competitor Dande and Gorillander
emerge victorious from the incredible aerial battle!

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.240
Return, Negigaknight!

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.070
Thanks for everything.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.450
Good showing, Gorillander!

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.790
Now you’ve done it,
supreme jerk!

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.670
Gah! Why’d he have to
pick up steam?!

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.040
It’s not over yet!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.630
He still has
Pikachu and Uonoragon, meow!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:36.060
Satoshi! You’ve given me and my Pokémon
a chance to show off our full potential.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.060
And yet, I’m sad.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.020
You have two Pokémon left.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.230
This incredibly exciting battle...

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.940
...is almost over.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.240
It’s not over till it’s over,
Mr. Dande!

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.240
Come out, Uonoragon!

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.410
Uonoragon!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.290
Its spikes are still morphed!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.630
Ice Fang!

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.210
Drum Attack!

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.910
What’s this?!
The Drum Attack was smashed to bits!

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.740
Now, Uonoragon!
Dragon Dive!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.040
100,000 Horsepower!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.820
Gorillander is unable to battle!

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.030
All right! We did it!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:19.910
And suddenly,
Competitor Satoshi closes the gap!

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.200
Return, Gorillander.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.580
You fought well.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.050
Uonoragon,
don’t let your guard down!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.720
Come out, Aceburn!

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.430
Aceburn arrives!

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.560
So it’s back...!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.790
Aceburn, the Pokémon
he kicked off the finals with.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:10.630
It has the ability Libero, which changes its own type
to that of the moves it uses.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.300
High Jump Kick!

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.760
It became a Fighting type!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:26.680
High Jump Kick lands!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:28.890
Water Gun!

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.730
Pyro Ball!

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.870
Pyro Ball cancels out
the Water Gun!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.200
Jaw Bite!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.080
Iron Head!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.550
Now it’s a Steel type!

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.180
Nice header!

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:03.180
Competitor Dande’s
completely setting the pace.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.980
Uonoragon, you okay?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.570
We’ll land the next hit!
Dragon Dive!

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:24.950
High Jump Kick!

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.230
Uonoragon is unable to battle!

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.230
Aceburn overwhelms Uonoragon!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.560
Return, Uonoragon!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.360
You did great.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.240
Is Satoshi going to be okay?

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:05.280
It’ll be fine!
Satoshi and the team will be fine!

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:10.370
You battled well. Return!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.580
Satoshi, this is my sixth Pokémon.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.090
Come out, Lizardon!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:28.890
Competitor Dande’s
supreme partner, Lizardon!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:34.650
Mr. Dande wants to finish the battle
with Lizardon.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.230
I’m counting on you, Pikachu!

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:41.240
Left with only Pikachu,

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:45.280
will Competitor Satoshi
be able to take down Lizardon?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:50.160
Or will Competitor Dande
bring the battle to a close?

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:50.990
Satoshi.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.540
Lizardon was my first Pokémon.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:15:00.130
My irreplaceable partner,
who’s always traveled with me.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:05.300
My first battle, my first catch,
my first evolution...

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.720
He’s been there
for everything and anything.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.260
We’re the same, Mr. Dande!

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:13.230
Me, I’ve always traveled
with Pikachu.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.640
And that’s why I wanna beat
Lizardon with Pikachu!

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.820
That’s why...
I’ll win with Lizardon!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.790
Kyodaimax!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:43.880
All right! Do it, Lizardon!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.640
It’s huge!

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.890
It’ll squash Pikachu flat!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.640
Wait— I... I can’t process this!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:05.940
Let’s go, Pikachu!
100,000 Volts!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.660
Dai Rock!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.080
Jump, Pikachu!

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:32.260
Dai Rock’s effect
whipped up a sandstorm!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:37.730
Despite its depleting stamina,
Pikachu rises above Lizardon!

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.140
Iron Tail!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.620
Dai Dragoon!

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:08.720
Pikachu!

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.090
It landed!

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:27.110
Good job hanging on.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:30.450
Kyodaimax’s power
really is something else.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.370
This is the <i>only</i> way
I can stand up to it.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.130
Pikachu!
Let’s use our full power!

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.260
I’ve been waiting for this!

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:04.270
Competitor Satoshi
activates his Z-Move!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.400
Far greater than 100,000 Volts...
1,000,000 Volts!

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:15.030
No, way, <i>way</i> greater than that!
Our super full power!

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.880
Pikachu! 10,000,000 Volts!

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.970
It’s Champion time!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.310
Kyodai Hellfire!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.080
This is perfect, Satoshi!

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:05.710
I’ve always wanted to try this...
Kyodaimax versus Z-Move!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.960
Me too, Mr. Dande!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:13.590
Kyodai Hellfire versus
10,000,000 Volts!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:21.350
The tremendous energy
leaves the whole of Shoot Stadium shaking!

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.250
What is this
Galar particle reaction?

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.260
An event like this
has never been observed before.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.260
Mugendaina...

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:13.280
It couldn’t be—
The Black Night is happening again?!

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.680
Sonia, look...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:49.060
Right... The Kyodaimax
and Z-Move colliding...

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:52.190
Plus, the enormous power of
Mega Evolution...

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:56.690
Maybe having them shake this stadium—
this space— has caused this...

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.320
What is the meaning of this?!

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:04.700
Though the Kyodaimax has ended,
black clouds continue to swirl above us!

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.220
That cry...

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:34.690
In the midst of their white-hot battle,
Mugendaina has come flying in out of nowhere.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.270
What is it after?

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:10.950
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:14.960
The fiercely fought finals battle
concludes at last?!

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:18.960
But suddenly, racing through the sky,
Mugendaimeow arrives!

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:20.710
Wha—?! What about the battle?!

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:24.380
Dunno why you’re here,
but you better not butt in, stupid Mugendaidai!

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:25.590
Get out!

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:27.800
It’s “Mugendaina,” you know...

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.010
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:32.060
The Finals IV - “Partners”

00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:33.680
“Let’s all tune in, meow!”
